{"id":"ahikam","name":"Ahikam","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ahikam"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ahikam","text":"Brother of support = helper, one of the five whom Josiah sent to consult the prophetess Huldah in connection with the discovery of the book of the law (2 Kings 22:12-14; 2 Chr. 34:20). He was the son of Shaphan, the royal secretary, and the father of Gedaliah, governor of Judea after the destruction of Jerusalem by the Babylonians (2 Kings 25:22; Jer. 40:5-16; 43:6). On one occasion he protected Jeremiah against the fury of Jehoiakim (Jer. 26:24). It was in the chamber of another son (Germariah) of Shaphan that Baruch read in the ears of all the people Jeremiah’s roll."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1436","lemma":"גְּדַּלְיָה","xlit":"Gᵉdalyâh","gloss":"Gedaljah, the name of five Israelites","kjv":"Gedaliah","count":23,"share":0.61},{"strong":"H296","lemma":"אֲחִיקָם","xlit":"ʼĂchîyqâm","gloss":"Achikam, an Israelite","kjv":"Ahikam","count":20,"share":0.53},{"strong":"H3458","lemma":"יִשְׁמָעֵאל","xlit":"Yishmâʻêʼl","gloss":"Jishmael, the name of Abraham's oldest son, and of five","kjv":"Ishmael","count":19,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H5418","lemma":"נְתַנְיָה","xlit":"Nᵉthanyâh","gloss":"Nethanjah, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Nethaniah","count":14,"share":0.37},{"strong":"H8227","lemma":"שָׁפָן","xlit":"shâphân","gloss":"a species of rockrabbit","kjv":"coney","count":11,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H3110","lemma":"יוֹחָנָן","xlit":"Yôwchânân","gloss":"Jochanan, the name of nine Israelites","kjv":"Johanan","count":9,"share":0.24}],"verses":["2Kgs.25.22","Jer.39.14","Jer.40.5","Jer.40.6","Jer.40.7","Jer.40.8","Jer.40.9","Jer.40.11","Jer.40.12","Jer.40.13","Jer.40.14","Jer.40.15","Jer.40.16","Jer.41.1","Jer.41.2","Jer.41.3","Jer.41.4","Jer.41.6","Jer.41.9","Jer.41.10","Jer.41.16","Jer.41.18","Jer.43.6","2Kgs.22.12","2Kgs.22.13","2Kgs.22.14","2Chr.34.20","Jer.26.24","Jer.40.10","Jer.41.5","Jer.41.7","Jer.41.8","Je